// Title: Communication To LocaltoNet Tunneling Service Initiated - Linux
// Sigma ID: c4568f5d-131f-4e78-83d4-45b2da0ec4f1
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Andreas Braathen (mnemonic.io)
// Date: 2024-06-17 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1572, T1090, T1102
// Description: Detects an executable initiating a network connection to "LocaltoNet" tunneling sub-domains.
//   LocaltoNet is a reverse proxy that enables localhost services to be exposed to the Internet.
//   Attackers have been seen to use this service for command-and-control activities to bypass MFA
//   and perimeter controls.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of the LocaltoNet service.
// References:
//   - https://localtonet.com/documents/supported-tunnels
//   - https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/unc3944-targets-saas-applications
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/linux/network_connection/net_connection_lnx_domain_localtonet_tunnel.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceNetworkEvents
| where RemoteUrl endswith ".localto.net" or RemoteUrl endswith ".localtonet.com"
